invariant: INV-10
file: ct.h
catches: test/size-floor.sh
reason: ct.h stops refusing a size_t narrower than 32 bits. On a 16-bit
  target such as msp430, records_before_key_update's cast keeps only the
  low bits of the records an AES-GCM write key has left, up to 2^24 - 1,
  so ch_write sends a KeyUpdate every 65536 records. test/size-floor.sh,
  which requires ct.h to stop compiling for msp430, objects.

--- old
_Static_assert(SIZE_MAX >= 0xFFFFFFFFU, "chapulin needs a size_t of at least 32 bits");
--- new
